[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772787273","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2772787273","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2772787273,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lRWBJ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T14:41:29Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T14:41:29Z","body":"We usually do `Object::cast_to<T>()` for this purpose.\r\n\r\nI don't mind too strongly making that an explicit `Object::is_class<T>()`, especially if the implementation can be faster than `cast_to<T>`, but we have likely hundreds of occurrences of `Object::cast_to<T>()` used for that exact purpose that would need to be refactored too.\r\n\r\nI'm not too keen on `Object::is_class` in C++ behaving differently from the version bound to the scripting API, that's surprising and also problematic for godot-cpp, which uses the scripting API but aims to replicate the ergonomics of Godot C++ modules.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772787273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772881842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2772881842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2772881842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lRtGy","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T15:02:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T15:05:26Z","body":"> We usually do `Object::cast_to<T>()` for this purpose.\r\n> \r\n> I don't mind too strongly making that an explicit `Object::is_class<T>()`, especially if the implementation can be faster than `cast_to<T>`, but we have likely hundreds of occurrences of `Object::cast_to<T>()` used for that exact purpose that would need to be refactored too.\r\n\r\n`Object::cast_to<T>()` is better than `is_class` in some ways - for one, it makes it more obvious if something is calling the code twice. It should be about the same speed as `is_class` too, since it should compile to the same binary code, and it does protect against `nullptr`.\r\n\r\nI did consider just using `Object::cast_to`, but the fact that `is_class` exists is enough to invite people to use it. Besides, `of (object->is_class<T>)` is more readable than `if (Object::cast_to<T>(object)`. This is probably part of the reason we do have a lot of `is_class` users in the code base.\r\n\r\n> I'm not too keen on `Object::is_class` in C++ behaving differently from the version bound to the scripting API, that's surprising and also problematic for godot-cpp, which uses the scripting API but aims to replicate the ergonomics of Godot C++ modules.\r\n\r\nThe behavior is the same, it's just using a different method to get there :)\r\n\r\nHowever, I do see and agree with your concerns. I was just pondering whether `object->cast_to` might be a good alternative, but that may just invite people to use and forget `nullptr` safety checks. Perhaps just use `Object::cast_to` for the compatible callers and call it a day?\r\nEdit: I just saw that you offered `Object::is_class(object)`, that might not be a bad choice; it would at least help with readability.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2772881842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775299674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2775299674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2775299674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6la7Za","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T10:40:06Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T10:43:54Z","body":"Am I right in saying the string based version only makes sense for trying to find `GDExtension` classes, or calling from script (where the type is not available beforehand) rather than core?\r\n\r\nI'm struggling to find why you would call the by string version _at all_ from core, except in very limited circumstances (for a bound function). Indeed it seems a bug waiting to happen if any classes got renamed, whereas mentioning the type would be a compile error.\r\n\r\ni.e. I'm struggling in the diffs to work out whether any of those `is_class_by_name()` calls are necessary. Unless they are to avoid includes / compiling out modules or something.\r\n\r\nCan probably fix this up in 3.x too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775299674/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775309771","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2775309771","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2775309771,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6la93L","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T10:43:52Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T10:43:52Z","body":"> Am I right in saying the string based version only makes sense for trying to find `GDExtension` classes, or calling from script (where the type is not available beforehand) rather than core?\r\n> \r\n> I'm struggling to find why you would call the by string version _at all_ from core, except in very limited circumstances (for a bound function). Indeed it seems a bug waiting to happen if any classes got renamed, whereas mentioning the type would be a compile error.\r\n\r\nThere's another use case: preserving encapsulation, and reducing header dependencies which affect build time.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n```\r\ncore/variant/callable.cpp\r\n97:             if (!obj || !obj->is_class(\"Node\")) {\r\n```\r\n\r\n`core` can't depend on `scene` so it shouldn't include `scene/main/node.h`.\r\nSo deferring this to a string-based check helps preserve encapsulation with a minor hack compromise.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775309771/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775321109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2775321109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2775321109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lbAoV","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T10:48:47Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T10:49:06Z","body":"So for now I'd start with a separate PR that just changes the current uses of `is_class(String)` to `cast_to<T>()` when it's appropriate.\r\n\r\nThe few occurrences changed here are just minor mistakes that got past review, but we've actually done such cleanup passes in the past already, e.g. #57720.\r\n\r\nThen we can consider whether changing the Object API to:\r\n- Prevent future mistakes if we think they're frequent and problematic\r\n- Possibly replace all uses of `Object::cast_to<T>` for class checks by a different, clearer API\r\n\r\nBoth invite bikeshedding and ideally I'd prefer not to break compatibility by changing the behavior of `Object::is_class()` which is exposed to scripting.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775321109/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777192935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-2777192935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":2777192935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6liJnn","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T23:18:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T23:18:51Z","body":"Is it possible to introduce the new method as an overload? We could have `is_class(String)` and `is_class<Type>()`. It would preserve compatibility, and it's similar to the recent `get_instance()` change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777192935/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3329225003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104924#issuecomment-3329225003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104924","id":3329225003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Gb_Er","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T15:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T15:12:37Z","body":"Superseded by #110832","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3329225003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimiz